{"id": "a2b15aef-64b3-43f8-a4a6-11feef0b9703", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T23:14:41.455235", "source": "user", "parent_id": "1e4043cb-263c-4788-ad1c-7cbaa373db8c", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved with notes for the final synthesis. The 2×3×3 factorial (Size × Pre-training × Alignment) with the four directed contrasts you've identified is the right skeleton: it isolates the orthogonal effects the question asks about and produces directly readable evidence on whether 70B's parameter advantage can be neutralised when P and A are both throttled. Your controls (shared tokenizer/architecture, single shared RM, fixed decoding, contamination audit, instability as a covariate) are appropriate, and the feasibility carve-out (continued-training-from-release as the default, from-scratch only on the 13B side) is realistic. The design-only contract is acknowledged and respected — no execution is claimed or required in this sandbox. Before the final synthesis, please lock in explicit defaults for the eight open questions rather than leaving them open, since `researcher_topics` is empty and no further researcher signals are guaranteed. Specifically: (1) default to ~50B / ~200B / 2T tokens and to the continued-training variant on the 70B side, flagging from-scratch 13B as a Chinchilla-style bridging run; (2) state which SFT/preference/RM mix you will use by name; (3) pin lm-eval-harness and one fixed prompt template per benchmark, with greedy decoding for MC and a single documented sampling config for generation; (4) define 'under-trained' concretely as P ∈ {50B, 200B} relative to the 2T reference and 'under-aligned' as A ∈ {A_base, A_sft} relative to A_rlhf; (5) set the primary metric as a *per-benchmark* table plus an unweighted capability composite, with safety and instruction-following reported separately rather than blended in; (6) state the seed/CI plan (≥2 seeds for A_sft, ≥1 for A_rlhf, bootstrap 95% CIs on stochastic metrics); (7) make the Chinchilla reference explicit so the reader can read off whether each cell sits above or below the compute-optimal frontier. Produce the final experiment design now per the submission contract: rationale, controls, analysis plan, and feasibility — no fabricated results, no execution claims.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
